.TH PSSigmoid 3 2023-12-03 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSSigmoid

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/activation.h>

.I
void  
.br
\fBPSSigmoid\fR(\fIPSFloat *vec\fR, \fIPSFloat *dest\fR, \fIuint64_t len\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sigmoid activation function for vectors. Sigmoid is computed on vector \fIvec\fR of length \fIlen\fR and stored into vector \fIdest\fR. If \fIdest\fR is \fINULL\fR, results will be stored into \fIvec\fR itself.
.br
The \fIopts\fR argument can be used to change default acceleration used to compute results (see \fIPSMathOpts\fR).
.br
For info about sigmoid:
.br
  \fIhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigmoid_function\fR
.br
The equivalent function to be used with scalars is \fIPSSigmoidS\fR.
.br
The derivative of this function is \fIPSSigmoidDerivative\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
PSSigmoidDerivative(3), PSSigmoidS(3)
